beam_process: pin the delivery fast path + capacity-retaining wake drain

Phase B (PERF BATCH 52 item 7) follow-up: integration evidence for the two
delivery-path work reductions plus the perf record.

tests/service_signals_fast_path.rs (6 cases) pins the observables on both sides
of the schedule-in fast path: a quiet schedule-in is a no-op (survives, state,
mailbox, links and collector counters untouched, no wake queued), an unknown or
stale pid is a no-op and never disturbs the recycled slot's occupant, a queued
signal is still applied in full, and a queued fatal signal still drives the whole
link cascade (head dies -> non-trapping middle dies -> trapping tail gets its
EXIT) -- the worklist only grows from a signal encountered while servicing, so
the fast path cannot shorten the cascade. drain_woken_into agrees with
drain_woken on the same scenario, clears a reused buffer instead of appending,
and the Scheduler's reusable wake scratch never double-enqueues.

PERF.md is the current-state record of the process-side share of end-to-end
send_recv: Method, Baseline (before), After (three runs with loadavg, the
load-matched before/after table and the floor-normalised movement), the ratios
with both sides named, the three-way attribution and the end-to-end arithmetic.

